# What `docker build ... apps/api` does not send to the builder.
#
# This file is the one that applies: every image of this project is built with
# its own directory as the context (`docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile
# apps/api`, and the same in the compose files and CI), and Docker reads the
# ignore file at the root of the context. The `.dockerignore` at the top of
# the repository is never consulted for it.
#
# It matters because the production image does `COPY . .`: whatever is in this
# directory on the machine that builds is in the image. CI builds from a clean
# checkout; a workstation does not. Before this file, an image built on one
# carried its `media/` -- every uploaded photograph and receipt it happened to
# hold -- and a new `api_media` volume, which Docker fills from the image the
# first time, started out with them (D240 in docs/roadmap.md).

# --- written at run time, never part of the application ---------------------
# The Dockerfile makes these three, empty and owned by the app's user; a volume
# mounted over one takes that ownership.
media/
staticfiles/
logs/

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- caches and build litter -------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
*.sqlite3

# --- the test suite -----------------------------------------------------------
# Not in the production image: nothing at run time imports it. The test and
# development images do not copy the source at all -- it is mounted
# (docker-compose.test.yml, docker-compose.dev.yml) -- so they still have it.
tests/
conftest.py

# --- how the image is built ---------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.dev
.dockerignore

# --- editors / os --------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
